## Before class

1. **Have your pitch and demo performance-ready**, not in draft. Slides finished, on the laptop you'll present from. The demo running from `main` (what your `cp12-demo` tag will capture), already logged in, with its data loaded. A fallback ready if the live path breaks.
2. **Rehearse it at least once against a clock: 9 minutes, hard.** Roughly 2 for the need, 5 for the demo, 2 for what's next.
3. **Re-skim Guy Kawasaki's [*10/20/30 rule*](https://guykawasaki.com/the_102030_rule/).** The rules haven't changed since your first pitch; the stakes have.
4. **Reread <course-link type="assignment" id="cp12">CP12</course-link> and its rubric** on the <course-link type="page" id="pg-rubrics">Assignment Rubrics</course-link> page, plus your retrospective and your signed onboarding checklist. Today's questions lean on them.
5. **Want to watch your own run?** Bring a phone for the stand at the back, or set up a screen recording. It's optional.

